0,Kalinga language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalinga_language,"Language family. Austronesian. Malayo-Polynesian.Majukayang Kalinga (Madukayang): spoken in Tabuk, Kalinga Province and in Paracelis municipality, Mountain Province. 1,500 speakers as of 1990.,[6] Language status is 6a.","Kalinga, Majukayang",Austronesian
1,"Kalinga, Madukayang in Philippines people group profile ...Igorot Music - Melodigging1 - Creating Places through the Soundscape: A Kalinga Peace ...kalinga Songs - YouTube MusicAustronesian soundscapes : performing arts in Oceania and ...Austronesian Music - Melodigging",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/13198/RP,"Learn about the Kalinga, Madukayang in Philippines people group. Profiles include statistics, text, photo, map, progress indicator and language resources. Igorot music refers to the traditional musical practices of the Cordillera peoples of Northern Luzon in the Philippines, including the Ifugao, Kalinga, Bontoc, Kankanaey, Ibaloi, and related communities. Warfare and revenge killings define much of life for the Kalinga of the northern Philippines. Fears of war express themselves in a range of beliefs and values that include appropriate hospitality for visitors, taboos regarding travel and regulations about spirit-world interactions. Listen to kalinga Songs on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more. ""In Austronesia--the region that stretches from Madagascar in the west to Easter Island in the east--music plays a vital role in both the construction and expression of social and cultural identities. Yet research into the music of Austronesia has hitherto been sparse. Austronesian music is an umbrella term for the diverse musical traditions of Austronesian-speaking peoples, whose homelands stretch from Taiwan through Island Southeast Asia to Oceania and Madagascar.","Kalinga, Majukayang",Austronesian
